earning that I was going to have to relearn everything anyway, I learned lo=
jban instead, which appeared to be much more vital.  So I did, from the CLL=
.  I learned all the gismu, all their places, and use them.  And yes, I don=
't want to have to relearn them.  At my age, it's a heavy memory load.  Thi=
s same kind of discussion goes on all time with one of my other passions, t=
ournament Scrabble. Of necessity, they have to reissue the dictionary every=
 so often.  But the old-timers don't want to have to restudy lists that the=
y already spent a long time memorizing, to add new words to them (or much w=
orse, deletions from them).  The young bucks who are just starting out don'=
t care, because they are tabulae rasae anyhow   Same goes with lojban, back=
wards compatibility asi
de.  So of course you are right to expect pushback from the oldtimers about=
 the idea.
